  "name": "Question 45",
  "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=3\\sqrt[6]{3x+13}-6.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n3\\sqrt[6]{3x+13}-6=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt[6]{3x+13}-6 & =0 \\\\ 3\\sqrt[6]{3x+13} & =6 \\\\ \\sqrt[6]{3x+13} & =2 \\\\ (\\sqrt[6]{3x+13})^{6} & ={2}^{6} \\\\ 3x+13 & =64 \\\\ 3x & =51 \\\\ x & =17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we must check the answer by substituting it back into the initial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt[6]{3\\cdot 17+13}-6 & =0 \\\\ 3\\sqrt[6]{64}-6 & =0 \\\\ 3\\cdot 2-6 & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=17.$",
